    "caption": "💳 Someone put a $59.7 million AI supercomputer on eBay. Free shipping\n\nIT hardware seller Core 4 Solutions listed a decommissioned cluster of 300 server racks with 9,600 Nvidia A100 chips and 4,200 AMD processors. Price: $59,700,000, \"or Best Offer.\" FedEx Ground shipping costs nothing.\n\nThat's about 1.4 petabytes of memory. The A100 is a 2020 chip, but Tom's Hardware calls it a real budget option: a single new Nvidia rack costs up to $6.5 million (Blackwell) or $7.8 million (Vera Rubin), with long waitlists.\n\nIts rough math for the chips and memory alone comes to about $28 million.\n\n@aipost 🏴",
