    ],
    "caption": "Ask Google's AI Mode who won the 2020 election and it may not say\n\nInstead of naming Joe Biden, Google's AI search mode told users to check the Federal Election Commission's official results. Asked about 2016, it answered right away: Donald Trump.\n\nGoogle's standalone Gemini app, ChatGPT and Claude all named the 2020 winner in tests by Ars Technica. AI Mode often gave the answer when asked a second time, and answered straight away when Ars checked from other countries via VPN.\n\nGoogle says it's fixing it: \"Our systems verify election responses using news articles or AP data for recent elections, and historic records for older ones. There was a technical gap with 2020 – same is true for 2022 Senate races.\"\n\nThe US midterms are on Nov. 3.\n\n@aipost 🏴",
